"eEn":"Under the Zhou system, the Son of Heaven's territory was a thousand li square, divided into one hundred counties, each containing four commanderies. Thus the Commentary on the Spring and Autumn Annals says, “A senior grand officer receives a commandery.” At the beginning of Qin rule, thirty-six commanderies were established to oversee their counties. Formed from 邑, with 君 indicating the pronunciation.",
