"w":"",
"variants":[],
"indexes":[
"黍"
],
"rid":"sw:4444",
"eEn":"A sticky member of the grain group. It is planted at the season of Great Heat, and is therefore called 黍. Formed from 禾, with an abbreviated 雨 indicating the pronunciation. Confucius said: “Glutinous millet can be made into wine: grain enters water.” All characters in the 黍 class are formed with 黍.",
