"eEn":"Old; long-lived. A creature with its bones outside and flesh within. Formed from 它, because a tortoise's head resembles that of a snake. The entry claims that broad-shouldered creatures have no males, and that tortoises and turtles take snakes as their males. Its form depicts the feet, shell, and tail. All characters in the 龜 class are formed with 龜.",
