"eEn":"A jade token of investiture, rounded at the top and square at the bottom. A duke holds a 桓圭, nine cun long; a marquis holds a 信圭 and an earl holds a 躬圭, each seven cun long; a viscount holds a grain-patterned jade disc and a baron holds a rush-patterned jade disc, each five cun across. These are used in investing the feudal lords. Formed from two stacked 土 components. Among the ranks of Chu is the title 執圭, “jade-tablet holder.”",
